  "slug": "framework-skyrmionic-polarimetry-57b2",
  "summary": "Analytical and optimization methods now target complete, rather than partial, characterization of structured optical states.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the complete characterization of structured optical degrees of freedom. One preprint defines full-skyrmionic polarimetry and a multi-stage optimization framework that uses topological evaluating functions to measure optical skyrmions accurately. A second preprint analytically computes the full Laguerre-Gaussian spectrum of SPDC biphotons with a generating-function method, enabling efficient evaluation of high-dimensional entangled states. A third preprint, on backward-scattering photoelectron holography in polar CO driven by sub-cycle laser pulses, addresses molecular strong-field dynamics rather than light-state metrology. It is included because it separates forward and backward scattering fringes, but it does not share the light-state focus of the other two. What is new is the emphasis on exhaustive rather than partial characterization, signaled by the word full in two titles.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
